{"views": {"player": "You step out of the Med Bay and into the metallic spine of the Central Corridor, where exposed wiring and maintenance hatches smell faintly of ozone. Behind you, the overridden blast door of the Med Bay remains open, revealing the sterile, dimly lit ward and the bandaged, injured crew inside. Through the open door of the Docking Bay, the evac shuttle Kestrel sits clamped and quiet. Lt. Marek Kessler stands near the threshold, alert and strained in his station security uniform. He locks his eyes onto you and taps his shoulder-mounted comm-link. You speak directly to him: "Your loyal doctor edited those logs herself. I can prove it. Ask her." Lt. Kessler responds firmly, "You've been trying to force your way into secure systems since you docked, Auditor. If you actually have telemetry to submit, file it through the proper command channels. Otherwise, step away from the patient." A person of unremarkable appearance.; wearing: station security uniform, tactical belt, holstered sidearm; clothing state: alert, strained the person of unremarkable appearance.; wearing Taps the comm-link on his shoulder to establish a direct connection to Dr. Sennett, keeping his eyes locked onto Auditor Rennick..", "21": "You are on the Command Deck, the station's nerve center, where scorched insulation hangs in the air and terminal readouts flicker with unstable diagnostic data. Your terminal display shows local ports isolated under administrative lockout. Through the closed door leading to the Central Corridor, muffled voices carry. Over your active audio comm-link, a security lieutenant's voice comes through clearly: "Your loyal doctor edited those logs herself. I can prove it. Ask her." The lieutenant, whose voice is close to his transmitter, replies directly: "You've been trying to force your way into secure systems since you docked, Auditor. If you actually have telemetry to submit, file it through the proper command channels. Otherwise, step away from the patient."", "22": "You stand in the metallic spine of the Central Corridor, near the open blast door of the Med Bay where an injured crewmember lies bandaged on a cot. Exposed wiring and maintenance hatches line the walls, smelling faintly of ozone. Through the open door of the Docking Bay, the evac shuttle Kestrel is visible. A lean, sharp-eyed woman in a pressed charcoal Oversight field uniform, wearing an Auditor's ID badge and holding a data-slate, steps out of the Med Bay. Keeping your eyes locked on her, you tap your shoulder-mounted comm-link to establish an active audio connection to the Command Deck. The woman in the Oversight uniform speaks levelly: "Your loyal doctor edited those logs herself. I can prove it. Ask her." You reply firmly: "You've been trying to force your way into secure systems since you docked, Auditor. If you actually have telemetry to submit, file it through the proper command channels. Otherwise, step away from the patient." a lean, sharp-eyed woman in a pressed charcoal Oversight field uniform, an Auditor's ID badge at her collar and a data-slate in hand; wearing: Oversight formal uniform, Oversight identification badge; clothing state: clean, orderly the lean sharp-eyed woman in a I catch Kessler alone in the corridor.", "23": "The Central Corridor is a long, metallic spine with exposed wiring and partially open maintenance hatches smelling faintly of ozone. The Med Bay blast doors are open, showing a wounded crewmember lying on a cot inside. The Docking Bay door is open, showing the evac shuttle Kestrel clamped in place. A lean, sharp-eyed woman in a pressed charcoal Oversight field uniform with an Auditor's ID badge stands near a station security officer in a security uniform. The officer has his hand on his active shoulder comm-link. The woman in the Oversight uniform says, "Your loyal doctor edited those logs herself. I can prove it. Ask her." The security officer replies, "You've been trying to force your way into secure systems since you docked, Auditor. If you actually have telemetry to submit, file it through the proper command channels. Otherwise, step away from the patient." A person of unremarkable appearance.; wearing: station security uniform, tactical belt, holstered sidearm; clothing state: alert, strained a lean, sharp-eyed woman in a pressed charcoal Oversight field uniform, an Auditor's ID badge at her collar and a data-slate in hand; wearing: Oversight formal uniform, Oversight identification badge; clothing state: clean, orderly the lean sharp-eyed woman in a I catch Kessler alone in the corridor. the person of unremarkable appearance.; wearing Taps the comm-link on his shoulder to establish a direct connection to Dr. Sennett, keeping his eyes locked onto Auditor Rennick..

